{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791565091,"nonce":"mN7Dyr2CahwF3BB9TWLr9I9FGpo=","message":"Step 2 done locally in f5b8cec5a7809337d4c644395960f19f050ad381, not pushed: a text element's content can follow a signal in place.\n\n- Text::bound(Reactive\u003cString\u003e) takes a constant, a State\u003cString\u003e or a Computed\u003cString\u003e. A constant builds a plain text.\n- A change is queued with the new queue_text_update, applied by apply_partial_property_updates (the one drain, so every runner gets it with no per-runner change), and RenderTree::set_text_content updates the layout measure context, the drawn text and the measured_width the paint path compares to decide whether to wrap.\n- Updated text is decoded like the text it was built with (HTML entities).\n- A bound text that does not wrap is measured through a context instead of getting the fixed size an unbound one has, so its box follows its content. Wrapping text already was.\n- PropertyId::TextContent now has a writer. needs_text_remeasure is still computed but no runner reads it; layout runs anyway because TEXT sets needs_layout.\n\nCompatibility: PartialPropertyUpdate gained a public field, text_content. Code that builds one with a struct literal needs text_content: None; the queue_* functions are unchanged, which is what blinc_abi uses.\n\nTests: 7 in binding.rs (follows a signal in place, wrapping text grows taller, computed source, entity decoding, measured_width refresh, unchanged value, constant stays plain) and one drain test. Removing the measured_width refresh fails one; removing the measure-context update fails two.\n\nNext is step 3 (Display and the text style properties), then moving cn's display-only closures onto these: the slider value, reactive_node's labels and the button label.","files":null}]}